Study 8: Single‐blind, randomized, controlled trial of pelvic floor muscle training, electrical stimulation, vaginal 
cones, and no active treatment in the management of stress urinary incontinence
- Decision: INCLUDE | Confidence: high
- Rationale: RCT in women with urodynamic stress urinary incontinence. Has pelvic floor exercises arm and no treatment 
control. Meets criteria.

Study 9: Does pelvic floor muscle training abolish symptoms of urinary incontinence? A randomized controlled trial
- Decision: INCLUDE | Confidence: high
- Rationale: RCT in women with stress and mixed UI. Has 12-week PFMT arm and control group. Meets all criteria.

Study 10: Group session teaching of behavioral modification program (BMP) for urinary incontinence: a randomized 
