│ changes according to perineal pad weight testing, which was used for the objective assessment of incontinence. Long  │
│ term follow up of these patients, after 9 months from commencing treatment still showed that pelvic floor exercises  │
│ are the most effective nonsurgical treatment for this condition.Taylor & Francis Online"}, {"study_index": 25,       │
│ "title": "Controlled trial of pelvic floor exercises in the treatment of urinary stress incontinence in general      │
│ practice", "abstract": "The aim of this study was to assess the usefulness of pelvic floor exercises in the          │
│ treatment of urinary incontinence in women and to analyse the factors which determine a successful outcome. The      │
