  are to discuss the theories behind why PFM training is effective in treating SUI and to discuss each theory in the    
  framework of new knowledge of functional anatomy and examples of results from RCTs. There are three proposed          
  theories to explain the effectiveness of PFM training for SUI: 1) women learn to consciously pre-contract the PFMs    
  before and during increases in abdominal pressure (such as coughing, physical activity) to prevent leakage; 2)        
